rows=[(131, 'dinner-without-the-familiar-voice', 'Dinner without the familiar voice', 'The speaker grieves not only a mother but the changed experience of an everyday meal. A plain roti left on a plate allows that ordinary loss without an invented maternal likeness or a nostalgic food advertisement.', 'Horizontal 3:2 restrained gouache and pencil still life, oblique seated viewpoint. One plain stainless-steel plate on a modest grey-brown dining table at lower left holds a single ordinary roti, slightly irregular and flat, with a few plausible brown cooking marks. No glistening ghee, steam or inviting food styling. Rim forms a coherent ellipse with subdued reflected light. The table continues into a broad quiet area to the right; just the lower edge of an empty chair behind it, softly unresolved. Gentle neutral afternoon window light, warm grey, wheat and dull silver. No person, portrait, flowers, utensils arranged for display, extra dishes, logos or text. Let the meal feel quiet and unremarkable; no heavy gloom or theatrical memorial cues.'), (123, 'between-the-earth-and-the-sky', 'Between the earth and the sky', 'The airplane view briefly lightens the burden of age, but the speaker remains drawn back to earth. An incomplete ordinary window view keeps wonder within a believable journey without assembling every rainbow colour.', 'Horizontal 3:2 dry pastel with soft gouache study from a passenger seat, close view of a single aircraft window cropped along the left frame. Simple off-white rounded oval inner surround, wall plane quiet and shadowed at left; through the window pale blue upper sky and uneven soft cloud tops with a small muted peach reflection from low sun. Most window view remains calm blue-grey rather than a spectacular sunset. No plane wing, passenger, logos, instruments, text, stars or impossible rainbow. Window depth and curved frame physically coherent. Selective pastel edges, soft ordinary cloud density, one quiet warm accent. Preserve a sense of brief lightness rather than a travel advertisement.'), (135, 'water-ready-at-the-threshold', 'Water ready at the threshold', 'The Odia poem turns preparation for a friend into an inward cleansing of envy and resentment. Water waiting at the entrance can suggest that welcome without illustrating every ingredient or inventing the visitor.', 'Horizontal 3:2 transparent watercolor with spare graphite. Low oblique view of a simple swept Odia domestic entrance, modest unpainted terracotta water pot placed securely beside the left door jamb on a plain shaded cement veranda. Pot has a round belly, narrow open neck and believable rim, no ornate decoration. Door slightly ajar, dark quiet interior beyond; sunlit empty approach extends across right half. Clean everyday surfaces with only ordinary material variation, no picturesque decay. Soft reflected daylight on clay, grounded contact shadow. No person, hands, feet, ritual symbols, rangoli, flowers, temple architecture, labels or extra utensils. An unshowy preparation for a friend, intimate and expectant.')]
